y could move this forecast.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Colorado has leaned Democratic in recent presidential elections by roughly six points, and with the incumbent term-limited, neither party carries an incumbency advantage. No general-election polls, expert ratings, or market pricing are yet available for this race, so the outlook rests on the state's underlying partisan lean.\n\nPrimary-season headlines show progressive candidates defeating incumbent Democrats in Colorado, which raises questions about coalition cohesion heading into the general election. Still, there is no direct evidence of a shift in the state's overall partisan balance, so the race remains a moderate Democratic favorite with meaningful uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7597, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6966, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7137, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.701, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.713, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7202, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7103, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7097, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7338, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7139, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7218, "margin": 6.0}]}